## The one with the balcony

Eighteen square metres around a double bed, with French doors that open on to a balcony of your own. There is a small table and a pair of bistro chairs out there, looking across the street to the trees and the brick fronts opposite, and it is the thing that turns this from a room you sleep in to a room you sit in.

The bed is set into a wall clad in pale timber, with the wardrobe built into the same run and a panel of sage geometric wallpaper behind the pillows. The cover is a quilted teal that picks up the green in the paper. A desk runs along the wall by the doors with the coffee machine on it, there is a framed print above, and a black reading lamp is mounted on the wall beside the bed.

Because the doors are glazed the full height of the wall, the room takes light from early in the day and holds it. Curtains draw across when you would rather it did not.

The bathroom has a corner shower behind curved glass, a wall-hung basin, a heated towel rail and a lit mirror.

Safe, iron and wardrobe come as standard, alongside the seating area, television and coffee facilities in every room. Breakfast runs from 07:30 to 10:30 at the front of the hotel, 10% off when you have booked direct.
